{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mrbdu1p780p","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"observed delta map merges with model map per action instead of replacing it","summary":"Run 28 empirical geometry: _observed_delta_map (measured from real suite transitions, single step only) OVERRIDES the model delta per action, while actions with no observation yet keep the model fallback from _model_delta_map. A pure observed map was tried first and failed: early in a walk only the actions already stepped are measured (e.g. only DOWN), so replacing the model map blinded the greedy walk to every other direction and it ground into the step cap. Two more empirical findings: batch transitions must never feed the map (three stride 2 moves recorded as one transition read as a bogus stride 6 action; the _suite_single_step flags gate this), and pure greedy L1 steering oscillates between the two cells flanking a wall — the walk needs the blocked move memo plus a visited cell tabu tie break, neither of which filters an action out, so the step cap remains the termination bound.","category":null,"tags":[],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-07-08T01:11:38.011Z","vec":[-0.022756395861506462,-0.0671495795249939,0.08193276077508926,-0.014760537073016167,0.028195520862936974,0.03227299079298973,-0.05176489055156708,0.005486490670591593,0.031170528382062912,-0.002445983001962304,0.07338584959506989,-0.013798555359244347,-0.042758550494909286,-0.031729649752378464,0.005802693776786327,0.007215437479317188,-0.029119154438376427,0.0071070995181798935,-0.02600153163075447,-0.05178527906537056,-0.025441449135541916,-0.04503655806183815,0.015843970701098442,0.0438384935259819,-0.01971207559108734,0.07474321126937866,-0.03541739657521248,-0.020778503268957138,0.06406248360872269,-0.12910190224647522,0.07323289662599564,0.08279997855424881,-0.0009362066630274057,-0.008674063719809055,0.08299852907657623,0.038931213319301605,-0.0511196069419384,-0.022493727505207062,0.0026905585546046495,-0.